  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) On the basis of back bonding, smaller be the halide atom, more effective be the back bonding and show less tendency to accept pair of electrons<br />(ii) Size of halides increases down the group hence ability to accept pair of electrons increases down the group.<br />Hence, correct order of Lewis acid for boron-halides is<br /><math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>Bl</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>BBr</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>BCl</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>BF</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math>",
